    "text": "Akan oral tradition includes folktales known as Anansesɛm.",
    "topic": "Akan oral tradition"
  },
  {
    "text": "Before European colonialism, the Akan preserved history, beliefs, moral values, philosophical ideas, and social institutions through spoken forms.",
    "topic": "Akan oral tradition"
  },
  {
    "text": "Akan oral tradition is considered one of the richest systems of indigenous knowledge production in West Africa.",
    "topic": "Akan oral tradition"
  },
  {
    "text": "The Akan used proverbs, songs, riddles, dirges, praise poetry, and oral narratives to convey their cultural knowledge.",
    "topic": "Akan oral tradition"
  },
  {
    "text": "European colonialism introduced literacy to the Akan people.",
    "topic": "European colonialism and Akan oral tradition"
  }
]
